Z||000000||ChopTop||09-23-2001||12:33 PM||||Hi folks I need some help diagnosing an intermittent problem my wife is having on her Fiero.  <BR>It's a 88 4cy, automatic with approximately 119,000 on it.<BR>The problem started last week.<BR>1. Drove home for lunch (approximately 4 miles), when leaving car would not start, it would turn over but not start. She said it sounded like it was flooded so she depessed the floor pedal, wait a few minutes, turned the key and it started.<BR> 2. Drove a mile from work, went in to grab lunch, car wouldn't start, depressed pedal, wait a few moments, car started.<BR>3.  Drove 7 miles to a friend, came to a stop, car stalled out.  Depressed car pedal, waited, took a few tries to start it, but did start.<BR>4. Drove to shopping center (2 miles).  Came back out 5 minutes later, car would turn over but not start, followed same procedure, but car refused to start this time.  Retrieved car two hours later and car started right up.<BR>Any suggestions or ideas on where to start looking would be appreciated very much. Dan & Dora.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-23-2001||02:58 PM||||Check the wire service article in my cave.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||ocalafiero1||09-23-2001||06:13 PM||||I had similar problems, and tried a few things that eventually cleared it up.<P>-First (and cheapest) replace the plugs. I got rid of the platinums and put in regular old AC's, started right up.<P>- prior to that I rebuilt the TBI, it made a difference as far as fuel delivery.<P>IMO, try doing the plugs first, and possibly the wires. Those would be the cheapest easiest fixes, and it sounds as though that may be part of the problem, i.e. "flooding".||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||09-23-2001||09:05 PM||||Hey Dan!<BR>The car turns over but refuses to start?<BR>Could be O2 sensor or TPS...<BR>Did you check for codes?<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> ||||reg||1
